# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
data/
dist/
target/

# Cargo.lock IS TRACKED — do not re-add it here. The line this replaces was
# inherited from the upstream Candle fork, whose own comment read "Remove
# Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries".
# Fuel ships a [[bin]], has CI, and has a 30-56 minute kernel forge whose warm
# artifacts are keyed on the resolved dependency set — so an unpinned resolution
# costs an hour, not a rebuild. Measured 2026-08-13 (GAP-180): four checkouts of
# this repo held two different resolutions differing across ~1904 lockfile lines.
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html

# editor config
.helix
.vscode
.zed
.claude

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Coverage profiling data
*.profraw

*tokenizer*.json
*.npz

perf.data
flamegraph.svg
*.dylib
*.so
*.swp
*.swo
trace-*.json
# FUEL_TRACE=1 in llama-lazy-vulkan writes trace.json
trace.json
# Vulkan submit log dumps from ad-hoc debugging runs
submits*.log

fuel-wasm-examples/*/build
fuel-wasm-examples/*/*.bin
fuel-wasm-examples/*/*.jpeg
fuel-wasm-examples/*/audios/*.wav
fuel-wasm-examples/**/*.safetensors
fuel-wasm-examples/**/*.gguf
fuel-wasm-examples/*/package-lock.json
fuel-wasm-examples/**/config*.json
.DS_Store
.idea/*
__pycache__
out.safetensors
out.wav
bria.mp3
bria.safetensors
bria.wav
